				141,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Sky): Refine terminology for bundled workbench pipeline\n\nClarify the description of the bundling process in the README by replacing the phrase \"pipeline that pre-compiles\" with \"compilation pipeline that pre-compiles into...\" for grammatical precision. Also change \"core workbench\" to \"core workbench\" (lowercase) to maintain consistent terminology regarding the VS Code integration.\n\nThese minor edits ensure the documentation accurately reflects the technical flow where Vite/Rollup compile variants into specific chunks within the `Target/Static/Bundled/` directory, without altering any functional behavior.",
			"SHA": "c5c73cadc43632104cea487bfb5a23a91c41d32f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T21:54:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				141,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Sky): Rewrite documentation to detail bundled workbench pipeline and event bridge\n\nReplace the high-level overview in README.md with a comprehensive technical narrative detailing Sky's internal architecture. Elaborate on the bundled workbench pipeline (`Vite`/`Rollup` compilation), the `SkyBridge` event routing system (~2900 lines of IPC logic), and the specific loading sequences for A1 (Browser), A2 (Mountain), and A3 (Electron) variants.\n\nUpdate the component tree diagram to reflect the new `Function/Build/` utilities, `Bundled/` directory structure, and detailed `Electron/` polyfills. Clarify how `@codeeditorland/output` transforms are applied and how the isolation hook operates within the `Tauri` webview. Ensure all dependencies and environment variables are accurately listed.",
			"SHA": "c6e2b50f1413518c0c06dfc19628cc1424ada946"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T21:13:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				141,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Sky): Correct repository URLs in license and changelog references\n\nUpdate all GitHub repository links in README.md to point to the `CodeEditorLand/Sky` repository instead of `CodeEditorLand/Land`. This ensures that the License and Changelog references correctly resolve to the component's own repository structure, consistent with Sky being a standalone git submodule.\n\nThe changes affect the badge links, the license file URL, and the changelog file URL, removing confusion for contributors viewing the documentation directly in the Sky submodule.",
